When Elastic IP is CHARGEABLE?
 
Elastic IP is NOT attached to any instance
 Example: You allocated an EIP but didn’t attach it
 
Elastic IP is attached to a STOPPED instance
 Instance stopped = EIP idle = charge
 
More than one Elastic IP attached to the same instance
 First one is free, extra ones are charged
 
Elastic IP attached to resources other than EC2
 Like unused or mis configured setups.
